msgstr "Loads the Core Rule Set once for the whole instance instead of once per service. Faster to load with many services, but service-scoped modsec-crs configs are refused while it is on: create a global one and scope it with a Host rule instead."

msgid "settings.modsecurity.global_crs.title"
msgstr "Global CRS mode"

msgid "settings.modsecurity.limits.description"
msgstr "How much of a request body ModSecurity inspects, and what happens to a body that exceeds the limit. NGINX enforces MAX_CLIENT_SIZE first, so a limit above it has no effect."

msgid "settings.modsecurity.limits.title"
msgstr "Request body limits"

